 "summary": "The PR adds genuinely new material: no type-B root generators or Serre relations exist in Mathlib (Classical.lean has only typeB/JB/typeBEquivSo') or elsewhere in TauCeti, and it reuses lie_single_single, LieHom.map_ad_pow, LieSubalgebra.coe_ad_pow, ad_neg_pow_apply_eq_zero, Matrix.submatrix_single_equiv and CartanMatrix.B rather than re-deriving them. The existing sl2-based higher-Serre lemma requires [IsDomain K] [CharZero K] and IsSerreSystem.neg_swap requires a complete system, so neither is an available replacement over an arbitrary CommRing.",
